sands:8\n\nTen thousands:4\n\nThousands:1\n\nHundreds:0\n\nTens:7\n\nOnes:2\n\nSo combining these:\n\n7 (hundred millions) \u2192 700,000,000\n\n7 (ten millions) \u2192 70,000,000 \u2192 total so far 770,000,000\n\n6 (millions) \u2192 6,000,000 \u2192 776,000,000\n\n8 (hundred thousands) \u2192 800,000 \u2192 776,800,000\n\n4 (ten thousands) \u219240,000 \u2192776,840,000\n\n1 (thousands) \u21921,000 \u2192776,841,000\n\n0 (hundreds) \u21920 \u2192776,841,000\n\n7 (tens) \u219270 \u2192776,841,070\n\n2 (ones) \u21922 \u2192776,841,072.\n\nYes, so the total is 776,841,072.\n\nWait, but let me verify with another method. Maybe adding the numbers step by step:\n\n160,261,934\n\n+616,579,138\n\nLet me add them:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n4 +8 =12, write 2, carryover1.\n\n3 +3 =6 +1=7, no carryover.\n\n9 +1=10, write 0, carryover1.\n\n1 (thousands place of first number) +9 (thousands of second) =10 +1=11, so write 1, carryover1.\n\n6 (ten thousands) +7 (ten thousands) =13 +1=14 \u21924, carryover1.\n\n2 (hundred thousands) +5 (hundred thousands) =7 +1=8.\n\n0 (millions) +6 (millions) =6.\n\n6 (ten millions) +1 (ten millions) =7.\n\n1 (hundred millions) +6 (hundred millions)=7.\n\nSo yes, that gives the same result. So the answer should be 776,841,072.\n\nWait, but let me check with another approach, maybe breaking the numbers into parts.\n\n160,261,934 can be written as 160,000,000 + 261,934.\n\n616,579,138 is 600,000,000 + 16,579,138.\n\nAdding the millions first: 160,000,000 + 600,000,000 = 760,000,000.\n\nThen the smaller parts: 261,934 +16,579,138.\n\nWait, 261,934 +16,579,138. Let's compute that:\n\n261,934 +16,579,138.\n\nAdding 261,934 +16,579,138:\n\nFirst, 261,934 +16,000,000 =16,261,934.\n\nThen add 579,138: 16,261,934 +579,138.\n\n16,261,934 +500,000 =16,761,934\n\nThen +79,138: 16,761,934 +79,138 =16,841,072.\n\nSo total is 760,000,000 +16,841,072 =776,841,072. Same result. Okay, that matches. So the answer is correct.\n\nTherefore, the final sum is 776,841,072.\n</think>\n\n",
