=13 +1=14 (4, carry1)\nHundred thousands:2 +5=7 +1=8 (8)\nMillions:0 +6=6 (6)\nTen millions:6 +1=7 (7)\nHundred millions:1 +6=7 (7)\n\nPutting all together, the digits from right to left are 2,7,0,1,4,8,6,7,7. Wait, but when written as a number, it should be 776,841,72? Wait, no, let me arrange them properly. Wait, the digits are:\n\nStarting from the ones place (rightmost):\n\nOnes: 2\n\nTens:7\n\nHundreds:0\n\nThousands:1\n\nTen thousands:4\n\nHundred thousands:8\n\nMillions:6\n\nTen millions:7\n\nHundred millions:7\n\nWait, so the number would be 7 (hundred millions), 7 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 2 (ones). Wait, that can't be right. Let me write it out step by step.\n\nWait, perhaps I messed up the order. Let me think again. When adding, the digits are:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 4 +8 =12 \u2192 2, carryover 1\n\nPosition 2 (tens): 3 +3 +1 =7 \u2192 7, no carryover\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds):9 +1 =10 \u2192 0, carryover1\n\nPosition 4 (thousands):1 +9 +1 =11 \u21921, carryover1\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands):6 +7 +1 =14 \u21924, carryover1\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands):2 +5 +1 =8 \u21928, no carryover\n\nPosition 7 (millions):0 +6 =6 \u21926\n\nPosition 8 (ten millions):6 +1 =7 \u21927\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions):1 +6 =7 \u21927\n\nSo the digits from right to left (starting at ones) are:\n\n2 (ones), 7 (tens), 0 (hundreds), 1 (thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 8 (hundred thousands), 6 (millions), 7 (ten millions), 7 (hundred millions).\n\nSo writing the number from left to right (hundred millions to ones):\n\n7 (hundred millions), 7 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 2 (ones).\n\nTherefore, the number is 776,841,072?\n\nWait, let me check that again. Let's see:\n\nBreaking down the digits:\n\nHundred millions place:7\n\nTen millions:7\n\nMillions:6\n\nHundred thousands:8\n\nTen thousands:4\n\nThousands:1\n\nHundreds:0\n\nTens:7\n\nOnes:2\n\nSo combining these:\n\n7 (hundred millions) \u2192 700,000,000\n\n7 (ten millions) \u2192 70,000,000 \u2192 total so far 770,000,000\n\n6 (millions) \u2192 6,000,000 \u2192 776,000,000\n\n8 (hundred thousands) \u2192 800,000 \u2192 776,800,000\n\n4 (ten thousands) \u219240,000 \u2192776,840,000\n\n1 (thousands) \u21921,000 \u2192776,841,000\n\n0 (hundreds) \u21920 \u2192776,841,000\n\n7 (tens) \u219270 \u2192776,841,070\n\n2 (ones) \u21922 \u2192776,841,072.\n\nYes, so the total is 776,841,072.\n\nWait, but let me verify with another method. Maybe adding the numbers step by step:\n\n160,261,934\n\n+616,579,138\n\nLet me add them:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n4 +8 =12, write 2, carryover1.\n\n3 +3 =6 +1=7, no carryover.\n\n9 +1=10, write 0, carryover1.\n\n1 (thousands place of first number) +9 (thousands of second) =10 +1=11, so write 1, carryover1.\n\n6 (ten thousands) +7 (ten thousands) =13 +1=14 \u21924, carryover1.\n\n2 (hundred thousands) +5 (hundred thousands) =7 +1=8.\n\n0 (millions) +6 (millions) =6.\n\n6 (ten millions) +1 (ten millions) =7.\n\n1 (hundred millions) +6 (hundred millions)=7.\n\nSo yes, that gives the same result. So the answer should be 776,841,072.\n\nWait, but let me check with another approach, maybe breaking the numbers into parts.\n\n160,261,934 can be written as 160,000,000 + 261,934.\n\n616,579,138 is 600,000,000 + 16,579,138.\n\nAdding the millions first: 160,000,000 + 600,000,000 = 760,000,000.\n\nThen the smaller parts: 261,934 +16,579,138.\n\nWait, 261,934 +16,579,138. Let's compute that:\n\n261,934 +16,579,138.\n\nAdding 261,934 +16,579,138:\n\nFirst, 261,934 +16,000,000 =16,261,934.\n\nThen add 579,138: 16,261,934 +579,138.\n\n16,261,934 +500,000 =16,761,934\n\nThen +79,138: 16,761,934 +79,138 =16,841,072.\n\nSo total is 760,000,000 +16,841,072 =776,841,072. Same result. Okay, that matches. So the answer is correct.\n\nTherefore, the final sum is 776,8