umbers with commas for clarity:\n\nFirst number: 796,328,469\n\nSecond number: 132,964,169\n\nLet me align them:\n\n          796,328,469\n        + 132,964,169\n        --------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):\n\nOnes: 9 + 9 = 18. Write 8, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 6 + 6 = 12, plus 1 is 13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds: 4 + 1 = 5, plus 1 is 6. Write 6, no carryover.\n\nThousands: 8 + 4 = 12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands: 2 + 6 = 8, plus 1 is 9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nHundred thousands: 3 + 9 = 12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nMillions: 6 + 2 = 8, plus 1 is 9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nTen millions: 9 + 3 = 12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nHundred millions: 7 + 1 = 8, plus 1 is 9. Write 9.\n\nSo putting it all together, the sum should be 929,292,638?\n\nWait, let me verify with another method. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nAlternatively, let me add the numbers step by step again carefully.\n\nFirst number: 796,328,469\n\nSecond number: 132,964,169\n\nAdding digit by digit:\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\n1. Ones: 9 + 9 = 18 \u2192 8, carryover 1\n2. Tens: 6 + 6 = 12 + 1 = 13 \u2192 3, carryover 1\n3. Hundreds: 4 + 1 = 5 + 1 (carry) = 6 \u2192 6, no carry\n4. Thousands: 8 + 4 = 12 \u2192 2, carryover 1\n5. Ten-thousands: 2 + 6 = 8 + 1 (carry) = 9 \u2192 9, no carry\n6. Hundred thousands: 3 + 9 = 12 \u2192 2, carryover 1\n7. Millions: 6 + 2 = 8 + 1 (carry) = 9 \u2192 9, no carry\n8. Ten millions: 9 + 3 = 12 \u2192 2, carryover 1\n9. Hundred millions: 7 + 1 = 8 + 1 (carry) = 9 \u2192 9, no carry\n\nSo the digits from right to left are 8,3,6,2,9,2,9,2,9. Wait, but when written normally, it's 929,292,638?\n\nWait, let me reconstruct the number:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):\n\nPosition 0: 8\n\nPosition 1: 3\n\nPosition 2: 6\n\nPosition 3: 2\n\nPosition 4: 9\n\nPosition 5: 2\n\nPosition 6: 9\n\nPosition 7: 2\n\nPosition 8: 9\n\nSo the number is 9 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 9 (millions), comma, 2 