e answer should be that. Let me check once more with another method, maybe column addition:\n\nLet me write the numbers vertically:\n\n          405,113,796\n        + 730,909,864\n        ---------------\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:6+4=10, write 0, carry 1\nTens:9+6=15 +1=16 \u21926, carry1\nHundreds:7+8=15 +1=16 \u21926, carry1\nThousands:3+9=12 +1=13 \u21923, carry1\nTen-thousands:1+0=1 +1=2 \u21922\nHundred-thousands:1+9=10 \u21920, carry1\nMillions:5+0=5 +1=6 \u21926\nTen-millions:0+3=3 \u21923\nHundred-millions:4+7=11 \u21921, carry1\nBillions: carryover 1 \u21921\n\nSo the digits are 1 (billions), 1 (hundred millions), 3 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 0 (ones). So combining gives 1,136,023,660. Yep, that's correct. I think that's the right answer.\n</think>\n\n",
