n865412687:8\nSum:3+8=11 +1 (carryover) =12 \u21922, carryover1\n\nNow, since there's a carryover of 1 after the hundred millions place, we need to add a new digit at the billions place: 1.\n\nSo putting all the digits together from right to left (since we started from the right):\n\nThe digits we got, starting from the first position (ones) to the ninth, plus the carryover:\n\nPositions 1-9 plus the new billion digit:\n\nThe digits from each position after calculation (starting from ones to hundred millions):\n\nPosition1:2\n\nPosition2:6\n\nPosition3:2\n\nPosition4:1\n\nPosition5:7\n\nPosition6:0\n\nPosition7:7\n\nPosition8:0\n\nPosition9:2\n\nPlus the carryover 1 at the billion place.\n\nSo the total digits are:\n\nBillions:1\n\nHundred millions:2\n\nTen millions:0\n\nMillions:7\n\nHundred thousands:0\n\nTen thousands:7\n\nThousands:1\n\nHundreds:2\n\nTens:6\n\nOnes:2\n\nWait, maybe I need to arrange them properly. Let me list the digits in order from highest to lowest place:\n\nStarting with the billions digit (the carried over 1), then hundred millions (2), ten millions (0), millions (7), hundred thousands (0), ten thousands (7), thousands (1), hundreds (2), tens (6), ones (2).\n\nSo the number is 1,207,071,262?\n\nWait let me check:\n\nBreaking down:\n\nBillions place:1\n\nHundred millions:2 \u2192 so 1 (billion) + 200 million = 1,200,000,000\n\nThen ten millions:0 \u2192 1,200,000,000\n\nMillions place:7 \u2192 1,207,000,000\n\nHundred thousands:0 \u2192 1,207,000,000\n\nTen thousands:7 \u2192 1,207,070,000\n\nThousands place:1 \u2192 1,207,071,000\n\nHundreds:2 \u2192 1,207,071,200\n\nTens:6 \u2192 1,207,071,260\n\nOnes:2 \u2192 1,207,071,262.\n\nYes, so the total is 1,207,071,262.\n\nWait, but let me verify with another method to be sure. Maybe adding the numbers as whole:\n\n341,658,575 + 865,412,687.\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\nFirst, 341,658,575 + 800,000,000 = 1,141,658,575\n\nThen add 65,412,687:\n\n1,141,658,575 + 65,412,687.\n\nAdding 65 mill