      "index": 0,
      "text": " Okay, so I need to add these two big numbers: 721,785,238 and 122,585,810. Hmm, let me think about how to approach this step by step. First, I should probably write them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits by their place values. Let me visualize that.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The first number ends with an 8, and the second ends with a 0. Adding those gives 8 + 0 = 8. So the ones place of the sum is 8. \n\nNext, moving to the tens place. The first number has a 3, and the second has a 1. 3 + 1 is 4. So the tens place is 4. \n\nNow the hundreds place. The first number has a 2, and the second has an 8. 2 + 8 equals 10. Oh, wait, that's more than 9, so I need to carry over. I'll write down 0 in the hundreds place and carry over 1 to the thousands place.\n\nMoving to the thousands place. The first number has a 5, the second has a 5. Adding those gives 10, plus the carried over 1 makes 11. So I put 1 in the thousands place and carry over another 1 to the ten-thousands place.\n\nTen-thousands place: first number has an 8, second has an 8. 8 + 8 is 16, plus the carried 1 is 17. So write 7 here and carry over 1 again.\n\nNext is the hundred-thousands place. First number has a 7, second has a 5. 7 + 5 is 12, plus the carried 1 is 13. So 3 in this place, carry over 1.\n\nMillions place: first number is 1, second is 2. 1 + 2 = 3, plus the carried 1 makes 4. So 4 here, no carryover.\n\nTen-millions place: first number is 2, second is 1. 2 + 1 = 3. So that's 3.\n\nFinally, the hundred-millions place: first number is 7, second is 0 (since the second number is only 9 digits, the hundred-millions place is the first digit which is 1, wait, hold on. Wait, let me check the actual numbers again. Wait, 721,785,238 is 9 digits: 7 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 1 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 8 (ones). The second number is 122,585,810, which is also 9 digits: 1 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 2 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 0 (ones). \n\nWait, so when adding the hundred millions place: 7 (from first number) + 1 (from second number) = 8. So that's the leftmost digit. Let me go through each place again carefully to make sure I didn't mix up any digits.\n\nStarting over step by step:\n\nLet me write both numbers with their place values:\n\nFirst number: 721,785,238\nBreaking down:\n- Hundred millions: 7\n- Ten millions: 2\n- Millions: 1\n- Hundred thousands: 7\n- Ten thousands: 8\n- Thousands: 5\n- Hundreds: 2\n- Tens: 3\n- Ones: 8\n\nSecond number: 122,585,810\nBreaking down:\n- Hundred millions: 1\n- Ten millions: 2\n- Millions: 2\n- Hundred thousands: 5\n- Ten thousands: 8\n- Thousands: 5\n- Hundreds: 8\n- Tens: 1\n- Ones: 0\n\nNow adding each column from right to left (starting with ones):\n\nOnes place: 8 + 0 = 8. Write down 8.\n\nTens place: 3 + 1 = 4. Write down 4.\n\nHundreds place: 2 + 8 = 10. Write 0, carry over 1.\n\nThousands place: 5 + 5 = 10, plus the carried 1 is 11. Write 1, carry over 1.\n\nTen thousands place: 8 + 8 = 16, plus 1 is 17. Write 7, carry over 1.\n\nHundred thousands place: 7 + 5 = 12, plus 1 is 13. Write 3, carry over 1.\n\nMillions place: 1 + 2 = 3, plus 1 is 4. Write 4, no carryover.\n\nTen millions place: 2 + 2 = 4. Write 4.\n\nHundred millions place: 7 + 1 = 8. Write 8.\n\nPutting all together, the sum should be 844,371,048?\n\nWait, let me check again. Wait, when I added the hundred thousands place: first number's hundred thousands is 7, second is 5. 7+5=12, plus the carried 1 makes 13. So we write 3 and carry over 1 to the millions place. Then millions place: first number's millions digit is 1, second is 2. 1+2=3 plus the 1 carried over is 4. That's correct. Ten millions place: 2 (from first) + 2 (from second) =4. Hundred millions: 7+1=8. \n\nSo the digits from right to left are:\n\nOnes:8, tens:4, hundreds:0, thousands:1, ten thousands:7, hundred thousands:3, millions:4, ten millions:4, hundred millions:8. So the number is 844,371,048?\n\nWait, let me write the digits in order:\n\nStarting from the highest place, which is hundred millions: 8\n\nThen ten millions:4\n\nMillions:4\n\nHundred thousands:3\n\nTen thousands:7\n\nThousands:1\n\nHundreds:0\n\nTens:4\n\nOnes:8\n\nWait, that would be 8 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 8 (ones). So putting commas: 844,371,048. Hmm, but let me verify with another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can add the numbers using another approach. Let's see:\n\n721,785,238\n\n+122,585,810\n\nAdding them:\n\nStart from the right:\n\n8 + 0 =8\n\n3 +1=4\n\n2 +8=10 (carry 1)\n\n5 +5 +1=11 (carry 1)\n\n8 +8 +1=17 (carry 1)\n\n7 +5 +1=13 (carry 1)\n\n1 +2 +1=4 (no carry)\n\n2 +2=4\n\n7 +1=8\n\nSo the digits are 8 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 8 (ones). So yes, 844,371,048.\n\nWait, but let me check with another way. Maybe breaking the numbers into parts.\n\n721,785,238 can be written as 700,000,000 + 21,000,000 + 700,000 + 85,238.\n\n122,585,810 is 100,000,000 + 22,000,000 + 500,000 + 85,810.\n\nAdding them:\n\n700,000,000 + 100,000,000 = 800,000,000\n\n21,000,000 +22,000,000 =43,000,000\n\n700,000 +500,000 =1,200,000\n\n85,238 +85,810 = 171,048\n\nNow add all those together:\n\n800,000,000 +43,000,000 =843,000,000\n\n843,000,000 +1,200,000 =844,200,000\n\n844,200,000 +171,048 =844,371,048. \n\nOkay, that matches. So the answer is 844,371,048. I think that's correct. Let me just confirm once more with a calculator approach.\n\nAlternatively, adding digit by digit again:\n\nFirst number: 7 2 1 7 8 5 2 3 8\n\nSecond number:1 2 2 5 8 5 8 1 0\n\nAdding each column from right:\n\nOnes:8+0=8\n\nTens:3+1=4\n\nHundreds:2+8=10 (0, carry 1)\n\nThousands:5+5=10 +1=11 (1, carry1)\n\nTen thousands:8+8=16 +1=17 (7, carry1)\n\nHundred thousands:7+5=12 +1=13 (3, carry1)\n\nMillions:1+2=3 +1=4 (4, no carry)\n\nTen millions:2+2=4\n\nHundred millions:7+1=8\n\nSo the digits are 8 4 4 3 7 1 0 4 8, which is 844,371,048. Yep, that's consistent. So I think that's the correct sum.\n</think>\n\n",
