lace.\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the right, the digits are 7 (ones), 6 (tens), 7 (hundreds), 7 (thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 8 (hundred thousands), 2 (millions), 3 (ten millions), 2 (hundred millions), and 1 (billions). So the total should be 1,223,837,767.\n\nWait, let me check that again to make sure I didn't make a mistake. Let me add them another way. Maybe breaking them into parts. \n\nFirst number: 989,601,515\nSecond number: 234,236,252\n\nAdding the millions: 989 million + 234 million = 1,223 million.\n\nThen the thousands: 601 thousand + 236 thousand = 837 thousand.\n\nThen the ones: 515 + 252 = 767.\n\nSo combining those parts: 1,223,837,767. Okay, that matches. So I think that's correct. I don't see any errors in my steps. The key was handling the carryovers correctly, especially in the millions and ten millions places. Yeah, that seems right.\n</think>\n\n",
