51,869\n\nAdding them:\n\n367,962,176\n\n+388,451,869\n\nLet me add the millions first:\n\n367,000,000 + 388,000,000 = 755,000,000\n\nThen the thousands:\n\n962,000 + 451,000 = 1,413,000\n\nThen the remaining parts:\n\n176 + 869 = 1,045\n\nAdding all together:\n\n755,000,000 + 1,413,000 = 756,413,000\n\nThen add 1,045: 756,413,000 + 1,045 = 756,414,045. Okay, that matches the previous result. So the answer should be 756,414,045.\n\nWait, but let me check once more with another method. Maybe using column addition step by step again.\n\nLet me write the numbers aligned properly:\n\n          3 6 7 9 6 2 1 7 6\n        + 3 8 8 4 5 1 8 6 9\n        ---------------------\nStarting from the right (units):\n\nDigit 1 (units): 6 + 9 = 15 \u2192 5, carry 1\n\nDigit 2 (tens): 7 + 6 = 13 +1 =14 \u21924, carry1\n\nDigit3 (hundreds):1 +8=9 +1=10 \u21920, carry1\n\nDigit4 (thousands):2 +1=3 +1=4 \u21924, no carry\n\nDigit5 (ten thousands):6 +5=11 \u21921, carry1\n\nDigit6 (hundred thousands):9 +4=13 +1=14 \u21924, carry1\n\nDigit7 (millions):7 +8=15 +1=16 \u21926, carry1\n\nDigit8 (ten millions):6 +8=14 +1=15 \u21925, carry1\n\nDigit9 (hundred millions):3 +3=6 +1=7 \u21927\n\nSo the digits from right to left are 5,4,0,4,1,4,6,5,7. So the number is 756,414,045. Yes, that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 756,414,045. I think that's right. Let me just do a quick check with approximate values. 368 million plus 388 million is roughly 756 million, which matches the starting digits. The rest of the digits add up to about 414 thousand and some, so the total makes sense. Okay, confident now.\n</think>\n\n",
