at again because I might have messed up the order.\n\nWait, actually, when writing the numbers, the first number is 171,939,526. Breaking it down:\n\n- Hundred millions: 1\n- Ten millions: 7\n- Millions: 1\n- Hundred thousands: 9\n- Ten thousands: 3\n- Thousands: 9\n- Hundreds: 5\n- Tens: 2\n- Ones: 6\n\nThe second number is 805,280,380:\n\n- Hundred millions: 8\n- Ten millions: 0\n- Millions: 5\n- Hundred thousands: 2\n- Ten thousands: 8\n- Thousands: 0\n- Hundreds: 3\n- Tens: 8\n- Ones: 0\n\nAdding each column:\n\nStarting from the right (ones):\n\n6 + 0 = 6\n\nTens: 2 + 8 = 10 \u2192 0 with carryover 1\n\nHundreds: 5 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 9\n\nThousands: 9 + 0 = 9\n\nTen thousands: 3 + 8 = 11 \u2192 1 with carryover 1\n\nHundred thousands: 9 + 2 + 1 (carry) = 12 \u2192 2 with carryover 1\n\nMillions: 1 + 5 + 1 (carry) = 7\n\nTen millions: 7 + 0 = 7\n\nHundred millions: 1 + 8 = 9\n\nSo putting all the digits together from right to left (since we started from the right):\n\nOnes:6, Tens:0, Hundreds:9, Thousands:9, Ten thousands:1, Hundred thousands:2, Millions:7, Ten millions:7, Hundred millions:9. \n\nWait, but when written as a number, it should be 9 (hundred millions), 7 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 6 (ones). So that's 977,219,906?\n\nWait, let me verify with another method. Maybe adding the numbers directly:\n\n171,939,526\n\n+805,280,380\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\nFirst, adding the millions:\n\n171,939,526 is 171 million plus 939,526.\n\n805,280,380 is 805 million plus 280,380.\n\nAdding the millions: 171 + 805 = 976 million.\n\nThen adding the remaining parts: 939,526 + 280,380.\n\nCalculating 939,526 + 280,380:\n\n939,526 + 200,000 = 1,139,526\n\n1,139,526 + 80,380 = 1,219,906\n\nSo total is 976,000,000 + 1,219,906 = 977,219,906. \n\nOkay, that matches the previous result. So the sum should be 977,219,906. Let me check once more with another approach, maybe breaking down each number into parts.\n\nAlternatively, using column addition:\n\nLet me write them vertically:\n\n\u2003171,939,526\n\n+805,280,380\n\n-------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 6 + 0 = 6\n\nTens: 2 + 8 = 10 \u2192 write 0, carryover 1\n\nHundreds: 5 + 3 = 8 + 1 (carry) = 9\n\nThousands: 9 + 0 = 9\n\nTen thousands: 3 + 8 = 11 \u2192 write 1, carryover 1\n\nHundred thousands: 9 + 2 = 11 + 1 (carry) = 12 \u2192 write 2, carryover 1\n\nMillions: 1 + 5 = 6 + 1 (carry) = 7\n\nTen millions: 7 + 0 = 7\n\nHundred millions: 1 + 8 = 9\n\nSo combining all digits from left to right: 9 (hundred millions), 7 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 6 (ones). So the number is 977,219,906. \n\nYes, that seems consistent. I think that's the correct answer. Let me just confirm with a calculator-like approach:\n\n171,939,526 + 805,280,380.\n\nAdding the two numbers:\n\n171,939,526\n\n+805,280,380\n\n= (100,000,000 + 70,000,000 + 1,000,000 + 900,000 + 30,000 + 9,000 + 500 + 20 +6)\n\n+ (800,000,000 + 0 + 5,000,000 + 200,000 + 80,000 + 0 + 300 + 80 +0)\n\nAdding each component:\n\n100,000,000 + 800,000,000 = 900,000,000\n\n70,000,000 + 0 = 70,000,000\n\n1,000,000 +5,000,000 =6,000,000\n\n900,000 +200,000 =1,100,000\n\n30,000 +80,000 =110,000\n\n9,000 +0 =9,000\n\n500 +300 =800\n\n20 +80 =100\n\n6 +0 =6\n\nNow adding all these together:\n\n900,000,000 +70,000,000 =970,000,000\n\n+6,000,000 \u2192 976,000,000\n\n+1,100,000 \u2192 977,100,000\n\n+110,000 \u2192 977,210,000\n\n+9,000 \u2192 977,219,000\n\n+800 \u2192 977,219,800\n\n+100 \u2192 977,219,900\n\n+6 \u2192 977,219,906\n\nYes, that's exactly the same as before. So the answer is definitely 977,219,906. I think that's solid. No mistakes in the steps. All methods cross-check to the same result. So I can confidently say that's the correct sum.\n</think>\n\n",
