(thousands), 7 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 6 (ones).\n\nAdding digit by digit from right to left:\n\nStarting with the ones place:\n\n4 + 6 = 10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nTens place: 5 + 0 =5 +1=6. Write 6.\n\nHundreds place: 0 +7=7. Write 7.\n\nThousands place:1 +3=4. Write 4.\n\nTen thousands place:3 +4=7. Write7.\n\nHundred thousands place:9 +8=17. Write7, carryover1.\n\nMillions place:7 +1=8 +1=9. Write9.\n\nTen millions place:3 +7=10. Write0, carryover1.\n\nHundred millions place:1 +8=9 +1=10. Write0, carryover1.\n\nNow, the carryover1 goes to the next place (billions), so total is 1 followed by the digits we wrote: 1 0 0 9 7 7 4 7 6 0?\n\nWait, let me see:\n\nWait, the digits we wrote from right to left are:\n\n0 (ones), 6 (tens),7 (hundreds),4 (thousands),7 (ten thousands),7 (hundred thousands),9 (millions),0 (ten millions),0 (hundred millions), and then the 1 in billions.\n\nWait, maybe I need to list them in order:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):\n\nAfter adding each place:\n\nOnes:0\n\nTens:6\n\nHundreds:7\n\nThousands:4\n\nTen thousands:7\n\nHundred thousands:7\n\nMillions:9\n\nTen millions:0 (with a carryover 1)\n\nHundred millions:0 (from 1+8+1 carryover? Wait, let me retrace.\n\nWait, the hundred millions place: first number's hundred millions digit is 1, second is 8. So 1+8=9, plus the carryover from the previous (millions place which was 1). Wait, no, the carryover from the hundred thousands place was 1, right?\n\nWait, let me go step by step again carefully:\n\nStarting over:\n\nDigits positions (from right, starting at 1):\n\nPosition 1 (ones):\n\n4 +6 =10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):\n\n5 +0 =5 +1=6. Write 6, carryover 0.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):\n\n0 +7=7 +0=7. Write7.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):\n\n1 +3=4. Write4.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):\n\n3 +4=7. Write7.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):\n\n9 +8=17. Write7, carryover1.\n\nPosition7 (millions):\n\n7 (from first number) +1 (from second number) =8 + carryover1=9. Write9, carryover0.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):\n\n3 (first) +7 (second)=10. Write0, carryover1.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):\n\n1 (first) +8 (second)=9 + carryover1=10. Write0, carryover1.\n\nNow, since there are no more digits, we add the final carryover1 to the next (billions) place.\n\nSo the total digits from right to left are:\n\n0 (ones),6,7,4,7,7,9,0,0, and then the 1 in the billions place.\n\nSo writing the number from left to right (billions down to ones):\n\n1 (billions), 0 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 9 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 0 (ones).\n\nWait, that would be 1,009,774,760.\n\nWait, let me check with another method. Maybe adding the numbers as whole:\n\n137,931,054 + 871,843,706.\n\nLet me add 137,931,054 + 800,000,000 = 937,931,054.\n\nThen add 71,843,706: 937,931,054 +71,843,706.\n\nAdding 70,000,000 to 937,931,054 gives 1,007,931,054.\n\nThen add 1,843,706: 1,007,931,054 +1,843,706.\n\nAdding 1,000,000 gives 1,008,931,054, then 843,706 more:\n\n1,008,931,054 + 800,000 =1,009,731,054\n\nThen +43,706: 1,009,731,054 +43,706 =1,009,774,760.\n\nYes, that matches. So the answer is 1,009,774,760.\n\nI think that's correct. Let me confirm once more with another approach.\n\nAlternatively, using column addition:\n\n          137,931,054\n        + 871,843,706\n        ---------------\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:4+6=10, write 0, carry 1.\n\nTens:5+0=5 +1=6.\n\nHundreds:0+7=7.\n\nThousands:1+3=4.\n\nTen thousands:3+4=7.\n\nHundred thousands:9+8=17, write7, carry1.\n\nMillions:7+1=8 +1=9.\n\nTen millions:3+7=10, write0, carry1.\n\nHundred millions:1+8=9 +1=10, write0, carry1.\n\nBillions: carry1.\n\nSo the result is 1,009,774,760. Yes, that's consistent. So the final answer is correct.\n</think>\n\n",
