ds: 7  \nTens: 9  \nOnes: 2  \n\nWait, let me arrange them properly. The digits from highest to lowest (billions down to ones):\n\nBillions place: 1  \nHundred millions: 3  \nTen millions: 3  \nMillions: 0  \nHundred thousands: 3  \nTen thousands: 6  \nThousands: 2  \nHundreds: 7  \nTens: 9  \nOnes: 2  \n\nSo combining these digits: 1,330,362,792. \n\nWait, let me check that again. Let's write each digit's place:\n\n- Billions: 1\n- Hundred millions: 3\n- Ten millions: 3\n- Millions: 0\n- Hundred thousands: 3\n- Ten thousands: 6\n- Thousands: 2\n- Hundreds: 7\n- Tens: 9\n- Ones: 2\n\nSo the number is 1,330,362,792. Let me verify this by adding the numbers another way. Maybe using another method.\n\nAlternatively, adding 940,174,722 + 390,188,070:\n\nLet me break them into parts. \n\nFirst number: 900,000,000 + 40,000,000 + 0 + 100,000 + 70,000 + 4,000 + 700 + 20 + 2  \nSecond number: 300,000,000 + 90,000,000 + 0 + 100,000 + 80,000 + 8,000 + 0 + 70 + 0  \n\nAdding each part:\n\nBillions: 900M + 300M = 1,200,000,000  \nTen millions: 40M + 90M = 130,000,000  \nMillions: 0 + 0 = 0  \nHundred thousands: 100k + 100k = 200,000  \nTen thousands: 70k + 80k = 150,000  \nThousands: 4k + 8k = 12,000  \nHundreds: 700 + 0 = 700  \nTens: 20 + 70 = 90  \nOnes: 2 + 0 = 2  \n\nNow adding all these together:\n\n1,200,000,000  \n+130,000,000 = 1,330,000,000  \n+0 = 1,330,000,000  \n+200,000 = 1,330,200,000  \n+150,000 = 1,330,350,000  \n+12,000 = 1,330,362,000  \n+700 = 1,330,362,700  \n+90 = 1,330,362,790  \n+2 = 1,330,362,792  \n\nOkay, that matches the previous result. So the sum is indeed 1,330,362,792. \n\nWait, but let me confirm once more with another method. Maybe using calculator-like addition:\n\n940,174,722  \n+390,188,070  \n= ?\n\nAdding the two numbers:\n\nStart from the right:\n\n2 + 0 = 2  \n2 + 7 = 9  \n7 + 0 = 7  \n4 + 8 = 12 (carry 1)  \n7 (ten thousands place of first number is 7?) Wait, let me write the numbers vertically:\n\n          9 4 0 1 7 4 7 2 2  \n        