\n\n7 (millions):7\n\n8 (ten millions):6\n\n9 (hundred millions):0\n\nPlus the carried-over 1 in the billions place (position 10).\n\nSo the number is 1,067,644,734?\n\nWait, let me check again:\n\nWait, the digits from right to left are:\n\nPosition 1 (ones):4\n\nPosition 2 (tens):3\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):7\n\nPosition4 (thousands):4\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):4\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):6\n\nPosition7 (millions):7\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):6\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):0\n\nPlus the carryover 1 in the billions place (position10).\n\nSo the number is 1 (billions), 0 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 4 (ones). So written as 1,067,644,734?\n\nWait, let me verify with another method. Maybe adding the numbers step by step.\n\nAlternatively, adding 436,064,957 + 631,579,777.\n\nLet me break them into parts:\n\n436,064,957 + 600,000,000 = 1,036,064,957\n\nThen add 31,579,777:\n\n1,036,064,957 + 31,579,777.\n\nAdding 30,000,000 gives 1,066,064,957.\n\nThen add 1,579,777:\n\n1,066,064,957 + 1,579,777.\n\nAdding 1,000,000: 1,067,064,957\n\nThen 579,777:\n\n1,067,064,957 + 500,000 = 1,067,564,957\n\nThen 79,777:\n\n1,067,564,957 + 70,000 = 1,067,634,957\n\nThen 9,777:\n\n1,067,634,957 + 9,000 = 1,067,643,957\n\nThen 777:\n\n1,067,643,957 + 777 = 1,067,644,734.\n\nOkay, so that matches the previous result. So the sum is 1,067,644,734.\n\nWait, but let me check once more with another approach. Maybe using column addition properly.\n\nLet me write both numbers:\n\nFirst number: 436,064,957\n\nSecond number:631,579,777\n\nAdding:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:7+7=14 \u21924, carryover1\n\nTens:5+7=12 +1=13 \u21923, carryover1\n\nHundreds:9+7=16 +1=17 \u21927, carryover1\n\nThousands:4+9=13 +1=14 \u21924, carryover1\n\nTen thousands:6+7=13 +1=14 \u21924, carryover1\n\nHundred thousands:0+5=5 +1=6 \u21926, no carryover\n\nMillions:6+1=7 \u21927\n\nTen millions:3