, 3 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 2 (ones). \n\nThe second number is 374,036,219, which is also 9 digits: 3 (hundred millions), 7 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 9 (ones). \n\nSo aligning them:\n\n          2 7 1 3 9 6 6 0 2  \n        + 3 7 4 0 3 6 2 1 9  \n        ----------------------\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\nOnes: 2 + 9 = 11 \u2192 1, carryover 1  \nTens: 0 + 1 + 1 (carry) = 2 \u2192 2, no carry  \nHundreds: 6 + 2 = 8 \u2192 8  \nThousands: 6 + 6 = 12 \u2192 2, carryover 1  \nTen-thousands: 9 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 13 \u2192 3, carryover 1  \nHundred-thousands: 3 + 0 + 1 (carry) = 4 \u2192 4  \nMillions: 1 + 4 = 5 \u2192 5  \nTen-millions: 7 + 7 = 14 \u2192 4, carryover 1  \nHundred-millions: 2 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 6 \u2192 6  \n\nPutting it all together, the sum should be 645,432,821. Wait, let me verify that again. Let me add them another way to cross-check. Maybe breaking them into parts.\n\nAlternatively, adding the numbers step by step:\n\n271,396,602  \n+374,036,219  \n= ?\n\nLet me add the millions first. 271 million plus 374 million is 645 million. Then the remaining parts: 396,602 + 036,219. Wait, 396,602 + 36,219. Let's compute that:\n\n396,602 + 36,219:\n\n396,602 + 30,000 = 426,602  \n426,602 + 6,219 = 432,821. \n\nSo total is 645,000,000 + 432,821 = 645,432,821. That matches the previous result. Okay, so that seems correct. \n\nWait, but let me check the thousands place again. In the original digit-by-digit addition, the thousands place was 6 (from first number) + 6 (from second number) = 12, so 2 with carryover 1. Then the ten-thousands place was 9 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 13, so 3 and carryover 1. Then hundred-thousands: 3 + 0 +1 =4. Millions: 1 +4=5. Ten-millions:7+7=14, so 4 and carryover 1. Hundred-millions:2+3+1=6. So yes, the digits are 6 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions),5 (millions),4 (hundred thousands?), wait, no. Wait, let me list all the digits from the addition:\n\nStarting from the right, the digits we got were:\n\nOnes:1  \nTens:2  \nHundreds:8  \nThousands:2 (with carryover)  \nTen-thousands:3 (with carryover)  \nHundred-thousands:4  \nMillions:5  \nTen-millions:4 (with carryover)  \nHundred-millions:6  \n\nSo putting them in order from left to right: 6 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 5 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands?), wait, let's see:\n\nWait, the places are:\n\nHundred millions: 6  \nTen millions:4  \nMillions:5  \nHundred thousands:4  \nTen thousands:3  \nThousands:2  \nHundreds:8  \nTens:2  \nOnes:1  \n\nWait, so the number would be 645,432,821. Yes, that's correct. So the final answer should be 645,432,821. I think that's right. Let me confirm once more with another method. Maybe using another breakdown.\n\nAlternatively, adding 271,396,602 + 374,036,219:\n\nLet me add 271,396,602 + 300,000,000 = 571,396,602  \nThen add 74,036,219: 571,396,602 + 70,000,000 = 641,396,602  \nThen add 4,036,219: 641,396,602 + 4,000,000 = 645,396,602  \nThen add 36,219: 645,396,602 + 36,219 = 645,432,821. \n\nYes, same result. Okay, so I'm confident the answer is 645,432,821.\n</think>\n\n",
