:9 +3 =12 \u21922 (carryover 1)\n8. Ten millions:3 +4 +1 =8 \u21928 (no carryover)\n9. Hundred millions:6 +3 =9 \u21929\n\nSo writing all the digits from right to left (since we started from ones):\n\nThe digits are:\n\nOnes:2\n\nTens:6\n\nHundreds:6\n\nThousands:6\n\nTen thousands:4\n\nHundred thousands:9\n\nMillions:2\n\nTen millions:8\n\nHundred millions:9\n\nSo putting them together: 9 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions), 2 (millions), 9 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 2 (ones). Wait, that would be 982,946,662?\n\nWait, let me check again. Wait, the digits from highest to lowest place:\n\nHundred millions:9\n\nTen millions:8\n\nMillions:2\n\nHundred thousands:9\n\nTen thousands:4\n\nThousands:6\n\nHundreds:6\n\nTens:6\n\nOnes:2\n\nWait, that would be 982,946,662?\n\nWait, but let me reconstruct the number step by step:\n\nStarting from the highest place (hundred millions):\n\n9 (hundred millions)\n\nThen ten millions:8 \u2192 so 980,000,000 + 80,000,000 = 980,000,000 + 80,000,000 = 1,060,000,000? Wait, no, that can't be. Wait, perhaps I'm mixing up the places.\n\nWait, actually, the digits are:\n\nHundred millions place:9 \u2192 900,000,000\n\nTen millions place:8 \u2192 80,000,000\n\nMillions place:2 \u2192 2,000,000\n\nHundred thousands place:9 \u2192 900,000\n\nTen thousands place:4 \u219240,000\n\nThousands place:6 \u21926,000\n\nHundreds place:6 \u2192600\n\nTens place:6 \u219260\n\nOnes place:2 \u21922\n\nAdding all these together:\n\n900,000,000\n\n+80,000,000 = 980,000,000\n\n+2,000,000 = 982,000,000\n\n+900,000 = 982,900,000\n\n+40,000 = 982,940,000\n\n+6,000 = 982,946,000\n\n+600 = 982,946,600\n\n+60 = 982,946,660\n\n+2 = 982,946,662\n\nSo the total is 982,946,662.\n\nWait, but let me verify this with another method to be sure. Maybe adding the numbers directly:\n\n639,274,549\n\n+343,672,113\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:9+3=12 \u2192 2, carryover 1\n\nTens:4+1=5 +1=6 \u21926, carryover 0\n\nHundreds:5+1=6 \u21926, carryover 0\n\nThousands:4+2=6 \u21926, carryover 0\n\nTen thousands:7+7=14 \u21924, carryover 1\n\nHundred thousands:2+6=8 +1=9 \u21929, carryover 0\n\nMillions:9+3=12 \u21922, carryover 1\n\nTen millions:3+4=7 +1=8 \u21928, carryover 0\n\nHundred millions:6+3=9 \u21929\n\nSo writing the digits from right to left as per the addition steps gives the same result: 982,946,662.\n\nHmm, but let me check with another approach. Maybe breaking the numbers into parts:\n\n639,274,549 can be written as 600,000,000 + 39,000,000 + 274,549\n\n343,672,113 can be written as 300,000,000 + 43,000,000 + 672,113\n\nAdding the large parts first:\n\n600,000,000 + 300,000,000 = 900,000,000\n\n39,000,000 +43,000,000 =82,000,000\n\nThen the smaller parts: 274,549 +672,113\n\n274,549 +600,000 = 874,549; 874,549 +72,113 = 946,662\n\nSo total is 900,000,000 +82,000,000 =982,000,000 +946,662 =982,946,662. \n\nOkay, that matches. So the answer should be 982,946,662. Wait, but let me confirm once more with a calculator-like approach.\n\nAlternatively, adding digit by digit again:\n\nFirst number: 6 3 9 2 7 4 5 4 9\n\nSecond number:3 4 3 6 7 2 1 1 3\n\nAdding each column from right (ones):\n\nColumn 1 (Ones):9+3=12 \u2192 2, carryover 1\n\nColumn 2 (Tens):4+1=5 +1=6 \u21926, carryover 0\n\nColumn3 (Hundreds):5+1=6 \u21926, carryover 0\n\nColumn4 (Thousands):4+2=6 \u21926, carryover 0\n\nColumn5 (Ten thousands):7+7=14 \u21924, carryover1\n\nColumn6 (Hundred thousands):2+6=8 +1=9 \u21929, carryover0\n\nColumn7 (Millions):9+3=12 \u21922, carryover1\n\nColumn8 (Ten millions):3+4=7 +1=8 \u21928, carryover0\n\nColumn9 (Hundred millions):6+3=9 \u21929\n\nSo the digits from right to left are 2,6,6,6,4,9,2,8,9 \u2192 which is 982,946,662. \n\nYes, that seems consistent. I think that's correct. I don't see any mistakes in the steps now. So the final answer should be 982,946,662.\n</think>\n\n",
