,259 + 780,963:\n\n400,000 + 700,000 = 1,100,000\n\n37,259 + 80,963 = 118,222 (since 37k +80k=117k, plus 259+963=1,222 \u2192 total 118,222)\n\nSo total of those two parts: 1,100,000 + 118,222 = 1,218,222.\n\nAdding that to the 525 million: 525,000,000 + 1,218,222 = 526,218,222. Okay, that matches the previous result. So the answer should be 526,218,222.\n\nWait, but let me check once more with another approach. Maybe using column addition:\n\n325,437,259\n+200,780,963\n-------------\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:9+3=12 \u2192 2, carry 1\nTens:5+6=11 +1=12 \u21922, carry1\nHundreds:2+9=11 +1=12 \u21922, carry1\nThousands:7+0=7 +1=8\nTen thousands:3+8=11 \u21921, carry1\nHundred thousands:4+7=11 +1=12 \u21922, carry1\nMillions:5+0=5 +1=6\nTen millions:2+0=2\nHundred millions:3+2=5\n\nSo writing the digits from right to left with carries, the final number is 5 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 2 (ones). So 526,218,222. That seems correct. I think that's the right answer. Let me just confirm with a calculator maybe? Well, since I can't use a calculator, but adding again:\n\n325,437,259\n+200,780,963\n= (300,000,000 + 25,437,259) + (200,000,000 + 780,963)\n= 500,000,000 + (25,437,259 + 780,963)\n25,437,259 + 780,963:\n25,437,259 + 700,000 = 26,137,259\n26,137,259 + 80,963 = 26,218,222\nSo total is 500,000,000 + 26,218,222 = 526,218,222. Yep, same result. Okay, confident now.\n</think>\n\n",
