s)\n\nDigit 2:8 (ten millions)\n\nDigit3:2 (millions)\n\nDigit4:2 (hundred thousands)\n\nDigit5:0 (ten thousands)\n\nDigit6:7 (thousands)\n\nDigit7:6 (hundreds)\n\nDigit8:9 (tens)\n\nDigit9:6 (ones)\n\nSecond number 278,834,434:\n\nDigit1:2 (hundred millions)\n\nDigit2:7 (ten millions)\n\nDigit3:8 (millions)\n\nDigit4:8 (hundred thousands)\n\nDigit5:3 (ten thousands)\n\nDigit6:4 (thousands)\n\nDigit7:4 (hundreds)\n\nDigit8:3 (tens)\n\nDigit9:4 (ones)\n\nNow adding each digit from right (digit9) to left (digit1):\n\nDigit9 (ones):6+4=10 \u21920, carry1\n\nDigit8 (tens):9+3 +1=13 \u21923, carry1\n\nDigit7 (hundreds):6+4 +1=11 \u21921, carry1\n\nDigit6 (thousands):7+4 +1=12 \u21922, carry1\n\nDigit5 (ten thousands):0+3 +1=4 \u21924, no carry\n\nDigit4 (hundred thousands):2+8=10 \u21920, carry1\n\nDigit3 (millions):2+8 +1=11 \u21921, carry1\n\nDigit2 (ten millions):8+7 +1=16 \u21926, carry1\n\nDigit1 (hundred millions):2+2 +1=5 \u21925, no carry\n\nWait, hold on, let me check digit3 again. Wait, digit3 is millions place. First number's digit3 is 2 (millions), second's digit3 is 8 (millions). So 2+8=10, plus the carry from digit4 (hundred thousands place which was 0+8+carry? Wait, maybe I messed up the order here.\n\nWait, let's go step by step again, carefully:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (digit9):\n\n1. Digit9 (ones): 6 +4 =10 \u2192 write 0, carryover 1\n\n2. Digit8 (tens):9 +3 +1=13 \u2192 write 3, carryover1\n\n3. Digit7 (hundreds):6 +4 +1=11 \u2192 write1, carryover1\n\n4. Digit6 (thousands):7 +4 +1=12 \u2192 write2, carryover1\n\n5. Digit5 (ten thousands):0 +3 +1=4 \u2192 write4, no carry\n\n6. Digit4 (hundred thousands):2 (from first number) +8 (second) =10 \u2192 write0, carryover1\n\n7. Digit3 (millions):2 (first) +8 (second) +1 (carry) =11 \u2192 write1, carryover1\n\n8. Digit2 (ten millions):8 (first) +7 (second) +1 (carry) =16 \u2192 write6, carryover1\n\n9. Digit1 (hundred millions):2 (first) +2 (second) +1 (carry) =5 \u2192 write5\n\nSo putting al