e digits would be:\n\nOnes:9\n\nTens:1 (with carryover)\n\nHundreds:3 (with carryover)\n\nThousands:2 (with carryover)\n\nTen thousands:5 (with carryover from previous?)\n\nWait, let me redo the step-by-step:\n\nLet me list each digit position:\n\nPositions (from right, starting at 1):\n\n1 (ones): 5 +4 =9\n\n2 (tens):2 +9=11 \u2192 1, carryover 1\n\n3 (hundreds):5 +7=12 +1=13 \u2192 3, carryover1\n\n4 (thousands):9 +2=11 +1=12 \u21922, carryover1\n\n5 (ten thousands):7 (from first number) +7 (from second number?) Wait, let me check the digits again.\n\nWait, maybe I need to write both numbers digit by digit properly.\n\nFirst number: 144,079,525\n\nBreaking down each digit from right (ones) to left (hundred millions):\n\nPosition 1 (ones):5\n\nPosition 2 (tens):2\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):5\n\nPosition4 (thousands):9\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):7\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):0\n\nPosition7 (millions):4\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):4\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):1\n\nSecond number:451,372,794\n\nBreaking down:\n\nPosition1 (ones):4\n\nPosition2 (tens):9\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):7\n\nPosition4 (thousands):2\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):7\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):3\n\nPosition7 (millions):1\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):5\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):4\n\nNow adding each position:\n\nPosition1:5+4=9\n\nPosition2:2+9=11 \u2192 1, carryover1\n\nPosition3:5+7=12 +1=13 \u21923, carryover1\n\nPosition4:9+2=11 +1=12 \u21922, carryover1\n\nPosition5:7+7=14 +1=15 \u21925, carryover1\n\nPosition6:0+3=3 +1=4 \u21924, no carryover\n\nPosition7:4+1=5\n\nPosition8:4+5=9\n\nPosition9:1+4=5\n\nSo putting all the digits together from position1 to position9:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (position1) to the left:\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):5\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):9\n\nPosition7 (millions):5\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):4\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):5\n\nPosition4 (thousands):2\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):3\n\nPosition2 (tens):1\n\nPosition1 (ones):9\n\nWait, that would make the number 595,452,319? Wait, let me arrange them properly.\n\nWait, the digits from highest to lowest place:\n\nHundred millions:5\n\nTen millions:9\n\nMillions:5\n\nHundred thousands:4\n\nTen thousands:5\n\nThousands:2\n\nHundreds:3\n\nTens:1\n\nOnes:9\n\nSo combining these: 5 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions), 5 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 9 (ones). So the number is 595,452,319?\n\nWait, let me check with another method. Maybe adding the numbers directly:\n\n144,079,525\n\n+451,372,794\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n5 +4 =9 (ones)\n\n2 +9 =11 \u2192 1, carryover1\n\n5 +7 =12 +1=13 \u21923, carryover1\n\n9 +2 =11 +1=12 \u21922, carryover1\n\n7 +7 =14 +1=15 \u21925, carryover1\n\n0 +3 =3 +1=4 \u21924, no carryover\n\n4 +1 =5\n\n4 +5 =9\n\n1 +4 =5\n\nSo yes, that gives 595,452,319. Wait, but let me confirm with another approach. Maybe breaking the numbers into parts.\n\n144,079,525 can be written as 144,000,000 + 79,525\n\n451,372,794 is 451,000,000 + 372,794\n\nAdding the millions parts: 144,000,000 +451,000,000 =595,000,000\n\nAdding the smaller parts:79,525 +372,794. Let's compute that:\n\n79,525 +372,794:\n\n79,525 + 300,000 = 379,525\n\n379,525 +72,794 = 452,319\n\nSo total sum is 595,000,000 +452,319 =595,452,319. That matches the previous result. So the answer should be 595,452,319.\n\nWait, but let me check once more with another method. Maybe using column addition:\n\n144,079,525\n\n+451,372,794\n\n------------------\n\nAdding each column:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:5+4=9\n\nTens:2+9=11 (1, carryover1)\n\nHundreds:5+7=12 +1=13 (3, carryover1)\n\nThousands:9+2=11 +1=12 (2, carryover1)\n\nTen thousands:7+7=14 +1=15 (5, carryover1)\n\nHundred thousands:0+3=3 +1=4 (4, no carryover)\n\nMillions:4+1=5\n\nTen millions:4+5=9\n\nHundred millions:1+4=5\n\nSo the result is 595,452,319. That seems consistent. I think that's correct. I don't