undred), 6 (ten), 9 (one). Wait, let me check that again because I might have messed up the places.\n\nWait, maybe I should write it out step by step more carefully. Let me list each digit position:\n\nLet me write both numbers with commas for clarity:\n\n783,944,466\n473,642,303\n\nAdding them:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 6 + 3 = 9\nTens: 6 + 0 = 6\nHundreds: 4 + 3 = 7\nThousands: 4 + 2 = 6\nTen-thousands: 4 + 4 = 8\nHundred-thousands: 9 + 6 = 15 (write 5, carry 1)\nMillions: 3 + 3 + 1 = 7\nTen-millions: 8 + 7 = 15 (write 5, carry 1)\nHundred-millions: 7 + 4 + 1 = 12 (write 2, carry 1)\nBillions: 1 (from the carry-over)\n\nSo putting it all together, the sum should be 1,257,586,769?\n\nWait, let me verify that. Let me add them using another method to cross-check. Maybe breaking them into parts.\n\nFirst number: 783,944,466\nSecond number: 473,642,303\n\nAdding the millions:\n\n700,000,000 + 400,000,000 = 1,100,000,000\n\n80,000,000 + 70,000,000 = 150,000,000 \u2192 total so far 1,250,000,000\n\n3,000,000 + 3,000,000 = 6,000,000 \u2192 1,256,000,000\n\nThen the next parts:\n\n944,000 vs 642,000: 944,000 + 642,000 = 1,586,000 \u2192 adding to previous total: 1,256,000,000 + 1,586,000 = 1,257,586,000\n\nThen the last part: 466 + 303 = 769. So total is 1,257,586,769. Okay, that matches my previous result. So the answer should be 1,257,586,769.\n\nWait, but let me check the digit-by-digit again to be sure. Let me write them aligned:\n\n          7 8 3 9 4 4 4 6 6\n        + 4 7 3 6 4 2 3 0 3\n        ---------------------\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\n6 + 3 = 9\n\nNext (tens): 6 + 0 = 6\n\nHundreds: 4 + 3 = 7\n\nThousands: 4 + 2 = 6\n\nTen-thousands: 4 + 4 = 8\n\nHundred-thousands: 9 + 6 = 15 (write 5, carry 1)\n\nMillions place: 3 + 3 = 6, plus the carry 1 makes 7.\n\nTen-millions: 8 + 7 = 15 (write 5, carry 1)\n\nHundred-millions: 7 + 4 = 11, plus the carry 1 makes 12 (write 2, carry 1)\n\nBillions place: only the carried 1.\n\nSo the digits from right to left are: 9,6,7,6,8,5,7,5,2,1. Wait, that would be 1,257,586,769. Yes, that's correct. So the final answer is 1,257,586,769. I think that's right. Let me confirm with another method, maybe using calculator-like addition.\n\nAlternatively, adding 783,944,466 + 473,642,303:\n\nLet me add 783,944,466 + 400,000,000 = 1,183,944,466\n\nThen add 73,642,303: 1,183,944,466 + 73,642,303\n\nAdding 70,000,000 gives 1,253,944,466\n\nThen 3,642,303: 1,253,944,466 + 3,642,303 = 1,257,586,769. Yep, same result. Okay, confident now.\n</think>\n\n",
