dreds: 9\n- Tens: 1\n- Ones: 4\n\nSecond number: 875,550,950. Breaking it down:\n- Hundred millions: 8\n- Ten millions: 7\n- Millions: 5\n- Hundred thousands: 5\n- Ten thousands: 5\n- Thousands: 0\n- Hundreds: 9\n- Tens: 5\n- Ones: 0\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake earlier. Let me recheck each digit step by step, starting from the right (ones place):\n\nOnes place: 4 + 0 = 4. Correct.\n\nTens place: 1 + 5 = 6. Correct.\n\nHundreds place: 9 + 9 = 18. So 8 with carryover 1. Correct.\n\nThousands place: 3 + 0 + 1 (carry) = 4. Correct.\n\nTen thousands place: 7 + 5 = 12. So 2 with carryover 1. Correct.\n\nHundred thousands place: 2 + 5 + 1 (carry) = 8. Correct.\n\nMillions place: 2 (from first number) + 5 (from second)? Wait, hold on. Wait, the first number's millions place is 2? Let me check again.\n\nWait, the first number is 742,273,914. Let's parse it properly:\n\nBreaking down 742,273,914:\n\n- 7 (hundred millions)\n- 4 (ten millions)\n- 2 (millions)\n- 2 (hundred thousands)\n- 7 (ten thousands)\n- 3 (thousands)\n- 9 (hundreds)\n- 1 (tens)\n- 4 (ones)\n\nSecond number: 875,550,950:\n\n- 8 (hundred millions)\n- 7 (ten millions)\n- 5 (millions)\n- 5 (hundred thousands)\n- 5 (ten thousands)\n- 0 (thousands)\n- 9 (hundreds)\n- 5 (tens)\n- 0 (ones)\n\nSo moving to the millions place: first number has 2 (millions), second has 5 (millions). So 2 + 5 = 7. Correct, no carryover.\n\nThen ten millions place: first number has 4, second has 7. 4 +7 =11. So that would be 1 in the ten millions place and carryover 1 to the hundred millions.\n\nWait, I think I missed that earlier. Let me go step by step again, maybe I skipped a place.\n\nWait, after the millions place comes the ten millions and hundred millions. Let me list all the places in order from right to left (since we add right to left):\n\nOnes: 4 +0 =4\n\nTens:1 +5=6\n\nHundreds:9+9=18 (8, carry 1)\n\nThousands:3 +0 +1=4\n\nTen thousands:7 +5=12 (2, carry1)\n\nHundred thousands:2 +5 +1=8\n\nMillions:2 +5=7\n\nTen millions:4 +7=11 (1, carry1)\n\nHundred millions:7 +8 +1 (carry)=16.\n\nWait, so the hundred millions place addition is 7 (from first number) +8 (from second) plus the carried over 1, totaling 16. So that would be 6 in the hundred millions place and carryover 1 to the billions place. Since both numbers are 9-digit numbers, their sum could be a 10-digit number. \n\nSo putting it all together:\n\nStarting from the ones digit:\n\n4 (ones)\n\n6 (tens)\n\n8 (hundreds)\n\n4 (thousands)\n\n2 (ten thousands)\n\n8 (hundred thousands)\n\n7 (millions)\n\n1 (ten millions)\n\n6 (hundred millions)\n\nplus the carried over 1 to the billions place, making it 1 in the billions place.\n\nSo the total sum would be 1,617,824,864?\n\nWait, let me verify that again. Let me write each digit step by step with the carries:\n\nLet me write both numbers aligned:\n\n          742,273,914\n        + 875,550,950\n        ---------------\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 4 + 0 =4\n\nTens:1 +5=6\n\nHundreds:9+9=18 \u2192 8, carryover 1\n\nThousands:3 +0 +1=4\n\nTen thousands:7 +5=12 \u2192 2, carryover1\n\nHundred thousands:2 +5 +1=8\n\nMillions:2 +5=7\n\nTen millions:4 +7=11 \u21921, carryover1\n\nHundred millions:7 +8 +1=16 \u21926, carryover1\n\nBillions: 0 (since both numbers are 9-digit) but the carryover 1 makes it 1.\n\nSo the final number is 1,617,824,864?\n\nWait, let me check the digits again:\n\nBillions place: 1\n\nHundred millions:6\n\nTen millions:1\n\nMillions:7\n\nHundred thousands:8\n\nTen thousands:2\n\nThousands:4\n\nHundreds:8\n\nTens:6\n\nOnes:4\n\nWait, that would be 1,617,824,864. Let me confirm by adding the numbers another way, maybe breaking them into parts.\n\nAlternatively, adding 742,273,914 + 875,550,950.\n\nLet me add the millions first:\n\n742,273,914 is 742 million plus 273,914.\n\n875,550,950 is 875 million plus 550,950.\n\nAdding the millions: 742 + 875 = 1,617 million.\n\nThen adding the remaining parts: 273,914 + 550,950.\n\n273,914 + 550,950:\n\n273,914 + 500,000 = 773,914\n\nThen add 50,950: 773,914 +50,950 = 824,864.\n\nSo total is 1,617,000,000 + 824,864 = 1,617,824,864. Okay, that matches. So the answer should be 1,617,824,864.\n\nWait, but in the initial step-by-step addition, when I added the hundred millions place, I had 7 +8 +1 (carryover from ten millions) =16, so that gives 6 in hundred millions and carryover 1 to billions. So the digits would be:\n\nBillions:1\n\nHundred millions:6\n\nTen millions:1 (from 4+7=11)\n\nMillions:7 (from 2+5)\n\nHundred thousands:8 (from 2+5+1)\n\nTen thousands:2 (from 7+5=12)\n\nThousands:4 (3+0+1)\n\nHundreds:8 (9+9=18)\n\nTens:6 (1+5)\n\nOnes:4.\n\nSo putting it all together: 1 (billion), 6 (hundred million), 1 (ten million), 7 (million), 8 (hundred thousand), 2 (ten thousand), 4 (thousand), 8 (hundred), 6 (ten), 4 (one). So 1,617,824,864. That seems correct.\n\nI think that's the right answer. Let me just do a quick check with approximate values. 742 million plus 875 million is roughly 1,617 million, which is 1,617,000,000. Then adding the remaining parts (273k +550k \u2248823k), so total is about 1,617,823,000. The exact answer is 1,617,824,864, which is close, so that makes sense. I think that's correct.\n</think>\n\n",
